<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila bourse serves ultimatum on mining firms.</title>
<headline>Manila bourse serves ultimatum on mining firms.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Stock Exchange (PSE) has threatened to suspend the trading of oil exploration and mining firms that fail to meet a requirement to increase the par value of their shares to at least one peso per share.</p>
<p>The PSE board of governors has approved a resolution giving the companies a deadline of August 12 to comply with the requirement, documents obtained from the PSE showed. Under the present set-up, the par value of a share can be as low as one centavo.</p>
<p>Setting the par value of shares at one peso will put Philippine issues at par with comparative companies in other Asian markets, PSE officials said.</p>
<p>((-- Manila newsroom (632) 841 8913 Fax 817 6267))</p>
</text>
